  "body": "Drawing radiant daylight into its interiors, this Gulf Harbour home stays spacious while balancing everyday practicality. Set across a 238m² floor plan on a 548m² section, its thoughtfully arranged spaces are designed for the family's daily rituals and elevated outlooks.\r\n\r\nGenerous glazing brings the surrounding landscape into focus, filling the living areas with natural light. The lounge, dining and kitchen flow together effortlessly, creating an inviting setting for family gatherings and entertaining. The central kitchen island anchors the space, while expansive windows frame leafy views and the neighbourhood beyond. A separate carpeted lounge provides another welcoming spot to unwind.\r\n\r\nFour well-proportioned bedrooms offer restful retreats, with carpet adding warmth underfoot and large windows drawing daylight. The main bedroom enjoys a leafy outlook and access to an outdoor deck, while the remaining rooms offer flexibility for family, guests or working from home. Three bathrooms, including contemporary tiled spaces with glass showers, support the rhythm of a busy household.\r\n\r\nOutdoor living unfolds across elevated decking, where morning coffees, leisurely afternoons and evenings with friends and whanau can be enjoyed against a green backdrop. A smaller balcony offers another place to pause and take in the views, while established greenery softens the 548m² grounds. A double garage and parking for two vehicles complete the practical appeal.\r\n\r\nGulf Harbour School and Wentworth College are within the wider neighbourhood, while weekends invite coastal walks through Shakespear Regional Park, beach outings and leisurely afternoons around Gulf Harbour Marina. With coastal recreation and everyday amenities within easy reach, contact Charlie Cochrane today!",
